B.afb=new A.ac(61488,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.bET=new A.dw("Research the Company","Understand their mission, values, products, and recent news. Know your interviewer if possible. This shows genuine interest.")
B.bF1=new A.dw("Analyze the Job Description","Break down the requirements and responsibilities. Match your skills and experiences to each point.")
B.bFd=new A.dw("Prepare Your Stories (STAR Method)",'For behavioral questions ("Tell me about a time when..."), prepare stories using the STAR method: Situation, Task, Action, Result.')
B.bFr=new A.dw("Prepare Questions for Them","Have at least 3-5 thoughtful questions ready. Ask about team culture, challenges, or what success looks like in the role. This shows you are engaged.")
B.bFq=new A.dw("Plan Your Outfit","Choose a professional and comfortable outfit. It's always better to be slightly overdressed than underdressed.")
B.bFl=new A.dw("Logistics Check","For in-person interviews, know the route and parking. For virtual interviews, test your camera, microphone, and internet connection. Ensure a clean, quiet background.")
B.b6q=s([B.bET,B.bF1,B.bFd,B.bFr,B.bFq,B.bFl],t.nt)
B.bEO=new A.pu("Before the Interview",B.afb,B.b6q)
B.bF8=new A.dw("First Impressions Matter","Be on time (5-10 minutes early). Offer a firm handshake (if in person). Be polite and friendly to everyone you meet, including the receptionist.")
B.bEU=new A.dw("Confident Body Language","Maintain good eye contact, sit up straight, and avoid fidgeting. Use hand gestures to emphasize points naturally.")
B.bFj=new A.dw("Listen Carefully","Pay close attention to the question being asked. It's okay to take a brief pause to structure your thoughts before answering.")
B.bFb=new A.dw("Be Concise but Thorough","Answer the question directly without rambling. Provide enough detail to demonstrate your expertise, using your STAR stories where appropriate.")
B.bEW=new A.dw("Show Enthusiasm","Express genuine interest in the role and the company. Smile and let your personality show.")
B.bFs=new A.dw("Ask Your Questions","When given the opportunity, ask the questions you prepared. This turns the interview into a two-way conversation.")
B.b4Z=s([B.bF8,B.bEU,B.bFj,B.bFb,B.bEW,B.bFs],t.nt)
B.bEP=new A.pu("During the Interview",B.wC,B.b4Z)
B.wz=new A.ac(61877,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.bFv=new A.dw("Send a Thank-You Note","Within 24 hours, send a personalized thank-you email to each person you interviewed with. Reiterate your interest and briefly mention something specific you discussed.")
B.bFu=new A.dw("Reflect and Take Notes","Jot down the questions you were asked and how you answered. Note any areas you could improve for future interviews.")
B.bF5=new A.dw("Be Patient","The hiring process can take time. Avoid pestering the recruiter. If you haven't heard back by the timeline they gave you, a polite follow-up email is appropriate.")
B.bFo=new A.dw("Handle Rejection Gracefully","If you don't get the role, reply thanking them and asking to be kept in mind for future openings. A gracious response keeps the door open \u2014 many people are hired from a company's \"silver medalist\" list later.")
B.aYL=s([B.bFv,B.bFu,B.bF5,B.bFo],t.nt)
B.bEQ=new A.pu("After the Interview",B.wz,B.aYL)
B.bEZ=new A.dw('"Tell me about yourself."',"This is not your life story. Use a Present-Past-Future structure: what you do now, the relevant experience that got you here, and why this role is your logical next step. Keep it under 90 seconds.")
B.bFw=new A.dw('"What is your greatest weakness?"','Pick a real but non-critical weakness, then show how you actively manage it. Avoid clich\xe9s ("I work too hard") and never name a weakness that is core to the job.')
B.bFm=new A.dw('"Why do you want to work here?"','Connect something specific about the company (a product, value, or recent move) to your own goals. Generic answers ("good reputation") signal you didn\'t do your homework.')
B.bF9=new A.dw('"Why should we hire you?"',"Summarize the 2-3 ways you uniquely match the job description, backed by a quick proof point. This is your elevator pitch \u2014 practice it out loud.")
B.bEY=new A.dw('"Where do you see yourself in 5 years?"',"Show ambition that fits a realistic growth path at the company. They want to know you'll stay and grow, not that you have a rigid, unrelated plan.")
B.b5f=s([B.bEZ,B.bFw,B.bFm,B.bF9,B.bEY],t.nt)
B.bEN=new A.pu("Common Questions & How to Answer",B.lv,B.b5f)
B.bF_=new A.dw("Lead With the Result","When you can, hint at the outcome early so the interviewer knows where the story is going, then walk through the Situation, Task, and Action.")
B.bFA=new A.dw("Conflict With a Coworker","Focus on how you sought to understand the other side, found common ground, and reached a professional resolution. Never badmouth anyone.")
B.bF2=new A.dw("A Time You Failed","Choose a genuine failure, own your part without blaming others, and spend most of your answer on what you learned and changed afterward.")
B.bF4=new A.dw("Leadership Without Authority",'Interviewers love examples where you influenced an outcome without being "the boss" \u2014 organizing a group project, mentoring a peer, or driving a decision.')
B.bFg=new A.dw("Quantify Everything",'Numbers make stories credible: "cut load time by 40%", "led a team of 5", "saved 10 hours/week". Even rough estimates beat vague claims.')
B.b3F=s([B.bF_,B.bFA,B.bF2,B.bF4,B.bFg],t.nt)
B.bEL=new A.pu("Behavioral Questions (STAR Deep-Dive)",B.lr,B.b3F)
B.afQ=new A.ac(984701,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.bFf=new A.dw("Think Out Loud","Your reasoning is being evaluated as much as the answer. Narrate your approach, assumptions, and trade-offs so the interviewer can follow and help you.")
B.bFe=new A.dw("Clarify Before You Solve","Restate the problem and ask about constraints, inputs, and edge cases before coding or calculating. Jumping straight in is a common red flag.")
B.bFz=new A.dw("Start Simple, Then Optimize","Get a brute-force or naive solution working first, then discuss how to improve time/space complexity. A working simple answer beats a broken clever one.")
B.bFk=new A.dw("Test Your Own Work","Walk through your solution with a small example and an edge case (empty input, max size, duplicates). Catching your own bug scores points.")
B.bF7=new A.dw("It's Okay Not to Know","If you're stuck, say what you do know and how you'd find the answer. Honesty plus a method beats bluffing.")
B.b82=s([B.bFf,B.bFe,B.bFz,B.bFk,B.bF7],t.nt)
B.bEM=new A.pu("Technical & Case Interviews",B.afQ,B.b82)
B.afA=new A.ac(62604,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.bF0=new A.dw("Look at the Camera, Not the Screen","To simulate eye contact, look into the webcam when you speak. Position the camera at eye level so you're not looking down at the interviewer.")
B.bFy=new A.dw("Light From the Front","Face a window or lamp; never sit with a bright window behind you, which turns you into a silhouette. Good lighting dramatically improves how you come across.")
B.bEV=new A.dw("Keep Notes Off-Screen","You can have a short bullet list (key stories, questions to ask) taped near your camera \u2014 but don't read from it. Glancing is fine; reading is obvious.")
B.bF3=new A.dw("Have a Backup Plan","Share a phone number in advance in case the video drops. If tech fails, stay calm \u2014 how you recover is itself a signal.")
B.bFh=new A.dw("Mind the Phone-Screen Basics","For phone screens, stand or sit up to project energy, smile (it carries in your voice), and remove all background noise and distractions.")
B.b6M=s([B.bF0,B.bFy,B.bEV,B.bF3,B.bFh],t.nt)
B.bEK=new A.pu("Virtual & Phone Interviews",B.afA,B.b6M)
B.afl=new A.ac(62054,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.bFn=new A.dw("Research the Range First","Use Glassdoor, Levels.fyi, and Levels for your role, level, and location before any number is discussed, so you have a defensible target.")
B.bEX=new A.dw('Deflect "What\'s Your Expectation?" Early',"If asked before an offer, it's fine to say you'd like to learn more about the role first, or to ask their budgeted range for the position.")
B.bFc=new A.dw("Negotiate on Total Compensation","Salary is one piece \u2014 consider signing bonus, equity, PTO, remote flexibility, and start date. There's often more room outside base pay.")
B.bFi=new A.dw("Counter Politely and With Reason",'Express enthusiasm for the role, then make a specific, justified counter. "Based on my research and experience, I was hoping for X" is professional and effective.')
B.bF6=new A.dw("Get It in Writing","Once you agree, ask for the full offer in writing before resigning from anything or declining other opportunities.")
B.b89=s([B.bFn,B.bEX,B.bFc,B.bFi,B.bF6],t.nt)
B.bES=new A.pu("Salary & Negotiation",B.afl,B.b89)
B.bFt=new A.dw("Lean on Projects & Coursework","No work history yet? Class projects, hackathons, research, and clubs are legitimate experience. Describe them with the same STAR rigor as a job.")
B.bFa=new A.dw("Highlight Transferable Skills","Part-time jobs, tutoring, and volunteering show reliability, communication, and teamwork \u2014 skills every employer values.")
B.bFx=new A.dw("Show You're Coachable","For internships and entry roles, attitude and willingness to learn often matter more than polish. Demonstrate curiosity and openness to feedback.")
B.bFp=new A.dw("Build and Bring a Portfolio","A GitHub, design portfolio, or writing samples give the interviewer something concrete to react to and set you apart from other new grads.")
B.aVv=s([B.bFt,B.bFa,B.bFx,B.bFp],t.nt)
